  "openDecisions": [
    "All notifications are in-app only. Email delivery and any email-reading or email-sending agent are explicitly excluded from this MVP at the owner's instruction, so memo_awaiting_approval will only be seen by someone who has the app open.",
    "Jobs run in-process inside the Node API rather than on a durable queue. An API restart mid-ingest leaves a Document stuck in parsing and it must be retried by hand. A real queue is the first infrastructure change needed before more than one person uses this concurrently.",
    "answer_question declares onFailure as run.no_evidence because a retrieval miss is the expected non-answer path. A genuine infrastructure error moves the run to failed instead, which is not modelled as an event because nothing downstream consumes it in MVP.",
    "The approve-to-export gate is enforced in the API, not just the UI: the download route re-checks memo state and approver role on every request. The MVP does not prevent the same person from generating and then approving their own memo when they hold the lead or partner role, it only records both actors. Whether INVRT needs genuine four-eyes separation is an open policy question.",
    "table.fill_completed fires even when some cells landed in not_in_corpus or unverified, which is why EvidenceTable has a partial terminal state alongside filled."
  ]
